## Implemented

Added a new reusable editor component at:

- `client/src/Components/common/JsonEditor.tsx`

### Features
- `Edit` enables editing mode
- `Save` parses JSON, updates local data, and calls `onSave(...)`
- `Cancel` reverts the editor back to the last saved JSON
- preserves the original JSON when not editing

### Usage

```tsx
import { JsonEditor } from "@/Components/common";

const MyComponent = () => {
  const [data, setData] = useState({ name: "example", enabled: true });

  return (
    <JsonEditor
      data={data}
      onSave={(updated) => setData(updated)}
      label="Monitor JSON"
      helperText="Edit the JSON and save changes."
    />
  );
};
```

### Notes
- It keeps `draftJson` while editing
- It validates JSON before save
- It updates displayed JSON after save

If you want, I can also add a small parent example into a page so you can see it in context.

